			"Message": "docs(Mist): Replace ASCII architecture diagram with Mermaid graph\n\nThe static ASCII art in `README.md` depicting Mist's DNS architecture was difficult to maintain and update. Replace it with a proper Mermaid `graph LR` diagram that uses semantic node styling and labels each module by its source file (Server.rs, Zone.rs, ForwardSecurity.rs, Resolver.rs, WebSocket.rs).\n\nThe new diagram adds explicit color-coded CSS classes for each subsystem (Mist, zone, forward allowlist, consumers, external), structures the layout into three labelled subgraphs (Land Components, Mist Local DNS Server, External), and uses directed edges to show the startup and query flow among Mountain, Cocoon, Air, and Mist. Component names now include emoji icons (🌫️, ⛰️, 🦋, 🪁, ☁️) for visual clarity.\n\nThis improves long-term maintainability of the documentation and makes the architecture immediately scannable for new contributors.",
			"SHA": "3ce319f67e175b46565e34ee628fe1cb512e9a5f"
		},
